WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.048
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEIC preparation.

2
00:00:05.348 --> 00:00:08.526
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.826 --> 00:00:17.062
Unit twelve: Part 5: Verb Tenses and Agreement. Today you will choose the correct tense and make subjects and verbs agree.

4
00:00:17.362 --> 00:00:19.992
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.933 --> 00:00:24.271
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.117 --> 00:00:25.944
Tense.

7
00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:29.635
Tense means the form of a verb that shows time.

8
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.576
Check the tense.

9
00:00:32.183 --> 00:00:34.580
Your turn. Say: Tense.

10
00:00:37.433 --> 00:00:38.295
Tense.

11
00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:39.993
Agreement.

12
00:00:40.983 --> 00:00:43.610
Agreement means matching the verb to the subject.

13
00:00:44.217 --> 00:00:46.344
Subject-verb agreement is tested.

14
00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:49.521
Your turn. Say: Agreement.

15
00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:53.414
Agreement.

16
00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.256
Singular.

17
00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:57.669
Singular means one.

18
00:00:58.283 --> 00:00:59.877
The manager is singular.

19
00:01:00.483 --> 00:01:03.078
Your turn. Say: Singular.

20
00:01:05.933 --> 00:01:07.039
Singular.

21
00:01:07.783 --> 00:01:08.483
Plural.

22
00:01:09.483 --> 00:01:10.995
Plural means more than one.

23
00:01:11.583 --> 00:01:13.118
The managers are plural.

24
00:01:13.717 --> 00:01:16.090
Your turn. Say: Plural.

25
00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:19.772
Plural.

26
00:01:20.517 --> 00:01:21.680
Present perfect.

27
00:01:22.683 --> 00:01:25.972
Present perfect means the tense for an action with a link to now.

28
00:01:26.583 --> 00:01:27.910
The company has grown.

29
00:01:28.517 --> 00:01:31.297
Your turn. Say: Present perfect.

30
00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:35.274
Present perfect.

31
00:01:36.017 --> 00:01:37.041
Passive.

32
00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:41.211
Passive means the form where the subject receives the action.

33
00:01:41.817 --> 00:01:43.236
The report was sent.

34
00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:46.816
Your turn. Say: Passive.

35
00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:50.610
Passive.

36
00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.421
Time marker.

37
00:01:53.417 --> 00:01:56.229
Time marker means a word like yesterday or since.

38
00:01:56.817 --> 00:01:58.433
Look at the time marker.

39
00:01:59.017 --> 00:02:01.715
Your turn. Say: Time marker.

40
00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:05.742
Time marker.

41
00:02:06.483 --> 00:02:07.450
Conditional.

42
00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:11.018
Conditional means about a possible situation.

43
00:02:11.617 --> 00:02:13.512
If we order, we will save.

44
00:02:14.117 --> 00:02:16.595
Your turn. Say: Conditional.

45
00:02:19.433 --> 00:02:20.388
Conditional.

46
00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:25.025
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.883 --> 00:02:28.324
Visal, how do I find the right tense?

48
00:02:29.417 --> 00:02:42.622
Look for a time marker, such as yesterday, since, by next week or currently. Yesterday needs the past simple, since needs the present perfect, and by next week often needs the future perfect.

49
00:02:43.717 --> 00:02:45.240
How is agreement tested?

50
00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:57.872
The subject may be far from the verb, for example, the list of new products is on the desk. The verb agrees with the subject list, not with products.

51
00:02:58.983 --> 00:03:00.867
What about passive questions?

52
00:03:01.983 --> 00:03:14.121
If the subject receives the action, use the passive: The invoice was sent yesterday. After a modal, use be plus the past participle, such as must be signed.

53
00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:16.721
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:17.583 --> 00:03:22.067
Grammar focus: Strategy: time marker, subject, passive.

55
00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:23.636
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:27.545
The company has grown since it opened in 2020.

57
00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.717
The list of new products is on the desk.

58
00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:38.020
Find the time marker, identify the true subject, and check whether the sentence needs an active or passive verb.

59
00:03:38.783 --> 00:03:42.376
Be careful! Don't say: I ignore time markers.

60
00:03:44.333 --> 00:03:46.762
Say: I use time markers.

61
00:03:47.062 --> 00:03:48.412
Time markers help.

62
00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.876
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:53.830
Time Markers.

64
00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:57.337
Sokunthea reads: The invoice ___ sent yesterday.

65
00:03:58.333 --> 00:04:00.484
Yesterday is a past time marker.

66
00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.521
The invoice does not send itself, so the passive is needed.

67
00:04:05.533 --> 00:04:07.986
The options are is, was, has and will.

68
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.535
She chooses was.

69
00:04:11.633 --> 00:04:15.728
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:16.583 --> 00:04:19.024
'Since 2020' needs the blank.

71
00:04:19.324 --> 00:04:23.570
A, present perfect. B, past simple. C, future.

72
00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:29.841
The answer is A: present perfect.

73
00:04:30.983 --> 00:04:34.399
In 'The list of new products blank on the desk', use blank.

74
00:04:34.699 --> 00:04:37.900
A, were. B, is. C, are.

75
00:04:41.433 --> 00:04:42.980
The answer is B: is.

76
00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:46.186
The invoice blank sent yesterday.

77
00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:49.710
A, has. B, will. C, was.

78
00:04:53.267 --> 00:04:55.440
The answer is C: was.

79
00:04:56.583 --> 00:04:58.246
A time marker is blank.

80
00:04:58.546 --> 00:05:03.686
A, a word showing time. B, a punctuation mark. C, a title.

81
00:05:07.233 --> 00:05:10.173
The answer is A: a word showing time.

82
00:05:11.317 --> 00:05:13.490
After a modal, the passive is blank.

83
00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:19.174
A, do + verb. B, be + past participle. C, is + base.

84
00:05:22.733 --> 00:05:25.847
The answer is B: be + past participle.

85
00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:30.080
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:30.917 --> 00:05:33.450
How do you choose the correct tense in Part 5?

87
00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:43.808
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:44.108 --> 00:05:56.179
I look for a time marker such as yesterday or since. I find the real subject and check the agreement, and I decide whether the sentence is active or passive. Then I choose the form that fits.

89
00:05:56.479 --> 00:05:58.072
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:58.983 --> 00:06:05.188
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: time marker, subject, passive.

91
00:06:05.488 --> 00:06:10.451
Today's value is logical rigor. Follow your reasoning wherever it honestly leads.

92
00:06:10.751 --> 00:06:13.450
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:16.483
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

